selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"#the-meanline\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">The meanline<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#the-meanline\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>The design runs at one mean radius through the whole turbine, so the blade\nspeed <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">u</span></code> is the same at every station. Give either <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">mean_diameter</span></code> or\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">blade_jet_ratio</span></code> (<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">u/c0</span></code>).</p><p>Each <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Stage</span></code> is a stator and a rotor. Its <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">flow_coefficient</span></code> (<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">c_x/u</span></code>) sets\nthe axial velocity through it. It also takes one of two things: <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">reaction</span></code>\n(the rotor\u2019s share of the stage\u2019s static enthalpy drop) or <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">exit_swirl</span></code> (the\nabsolute swirl leaving the rotor, in m/s). The other follows from it.</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/components/TurbineComponent.html#pyskyfire.viz.components.TurbineComponent\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.components.TurbineComponent\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.components.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">TurbineComponent</span></span></dt><dd><p>Display a built turbine: its passage walls and every row\u2019s blades.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">geometry</span></code> is a <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">TurbineGeometry</span></code>. Walls are\nthe passage revolved about the local +x shaft; each row\u2019s one built blade\nis repeated round the wheel in the turbine\u2019s rotation sense. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">colors</span></code>\npaints (stator, rotor) blades apart; without it every part takes the\ndefault colour. Optional <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">results</span></code> maps part names\n(hub, shroud, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">&lt;row&gt;_&lt;i&gt;</span></code>) to dictionaries of mesh-aligned FieldData.\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">inlet</span></code> and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">outlet</span></code> anchors sit on the axis at the passage ends,\npointing out of the turbine.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/turbine/duty/TurbineDuty.html#pyskyfire.turbine.duty.TurbineDuty\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.turbine.duty.TurbineDuty\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.turbine.duty.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">TurbineDuty</span></span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/thermo/duty/MachineDuty.html#pyskyfire.thermo.duty.MachineDuty\" title=\"pyskyfire.thermo.duty.MachineDuty\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.thermo.duty.MachineDuty</span></code></a></p><p>What a turbine is asked to do. See <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">MachineDuty</span></code>.</p><p>Build one with <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#pyskyfire.turbine.duty.TurbineDuty.from_states\" title=\"pyskyfire.turbine.duty.TurbineDuty.from_states\"><code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">from_states()</span></code></a> or <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#pyskyfire.turbine.duty.TurbineDuty.from_stations\" title=\"pyskyfire.turbine.duty.TurbineDuty.from_stations\"><code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">from_stations()</span></code></a>.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/turbine/axial/RowSettings.html#pyskyfire.turbine.axial.RowSettings\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.turbine.axial.RowSettings\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.turbine.axial.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">RowSettings</span></span></dt><dd><p>How the triangles become blades.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/turbine/axial/Stage.html#pyskyfire.turbine.axial.Stage\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.turbine.axial.Stage\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.turbine.axial.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Stage</span></span></dt><dd><p>The velocity-triangle choices for one stage.</p><p>Give <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">reaction</span></code> or <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">exit_swirl</span></code>, not both.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#design-an-axial-turbine\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Design an axial turbine<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#design-an-axial-turbine\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Blade generation needs pyTurbo, which comes with the impeller extra, and the\nscene needs the viz extra:</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/turbine/definition/BladeRow.html#pyskyfire.turbine.definition.BladeRow\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.turbine.definition.BladeRow\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.turbine.definition.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">BladeRow</span></span></dt><dd><p>One row of blades, as hardware.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/turbine/duty/TurbineDuty.html#pyskyfire.turbine.duty.TurbineDuty.from_states\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.turbine.duty.TurbineDuty.from_states\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">classmethod</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">from_states</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">fluid</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">mdot</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">p0_in</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">T0_in</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">p_out</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">n</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">outlet_basis</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'total'</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>A medium, a mass flow, the inlet total state and the outlet pressure.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">fluid</span></code> is a CoolProp name, a <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Fluid</span></code>, or\nany <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">EquationOfState</span></code>.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/scene/Scene.html#pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene.add\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene.add\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">add</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">component</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">transform</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">position</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">rotation</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">parent</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">anchor</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">attach_to</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">tags</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">()</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/turbine/axial/AxialTurbine.html#pyskyfire.turbine.axial.AxialTurbine\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.turbine.axial.AxialTurbine\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.turbine.axial.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AxialTurbine</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">duty</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">efficiency</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">stages</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">mean_diameter</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">blade_jet_ratio</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">work_split</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">inlet_swirl</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">loss_split</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">rows</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">rotation</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">COUNTERCLOCKWISE</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Design an axial turbine at mean radius. See the module docstring.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#the-definition\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">The definition<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#the-definition\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">turbine.definition</span></code> is a <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">TurbineDefinition</span></code>: hardware only. It holds a flat\ntuple of <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">BladeRow</span></code> (count, axial position and chord, annulus radii, metal\nangles and stagger at mean radius, thicknesses, clearances, admission, and a\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">twist</span></code> law), plus the <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">MeridionalPassage</span></code> through them. The passage records\nwhich walls turn and which blade gaps exist:</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/turbine/definition/TurbineDefinition.html#pyskyfire.turbine.definition.TurbineDefinition\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.turbine.definition.TurbineDefinition\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.turbine.definition.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">TurbineDefinition</span></span></dt><dd><p>An axial turbine\u2019s rows and the annular passage through them.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/index.html#module-pyskyfire.viz\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.viz<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.viz\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><h2>Submodules<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#submodules\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/turbine/index.html#module-pyskyfire.turbine\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.turbine<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.turbine\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Axial turbine design: the duty, a meanline design, and the hardware it produces.</p>", "a[href=\"#from-triangles-to-blades\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">From triangles to blades<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#from-triangles-to-blades\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">RowSettings</span></code> applies to every row:</p>", "a[href=\"#built-geometry-and-what-is-measured-on-it\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Built geometry and what is measured on it<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#built-geometry-and-what-is-measured-on-it\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">build_geometry(span_points=9,</span> <span class=\"pre\">chord_points=129)</span></code> draws each row\u2019s sections\nwith pyTurbo at their span radii. It stacks them on their centroids and wraps\nthem onto the annulus. A rotor\u2019s tips stop <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">tip_clearance</span></code> short of the\ncasing. Each <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">RowGeometry</span></code> holds one blade\u2019s suction and pressure surfaces, in\ncylindrical <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(x,</span> <span class=\"pre\">r,</span> <span class=\"pre\">theta)</span></code>.</p><p>These are measured on the built sections rather than given, at every span:</p>", "a[href=\"#plots\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Plots<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#plots\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz</span></code> has four Plotly figures for a turbine, ready for\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Report.add_figure</span></code>:</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/scene/Scene.html#pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.scene.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Scene</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">title</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'Pyskyfire</span> <span class=\"pre\">3D'</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">color_by</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">clim</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">show_axes</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">False</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Assemble components for desktop or standalone HTML display.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">anchor</span></code> names the added component\u2019s local anchor; <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">attach_to</span></code> is a\nworld-space Anchor. Attachment mates their outward x axes in opposition.\nIt is a one-time placement calculation, with no fluid-network constraints.\nExplicit placement and anchor placement are mutually exclusive.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">tags</span></code> labels the added node, a string or an iterable of them. Nodes\nsharing a tag appear together as one group in the HTML viewer, so a\ngrouping written into the script survives regenerating the results.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">show_axes</span></code> adds a corner orientation triad marking the scene axes\n(x red, y green, z blue). It is an orientation cue only, not a measuring\ngrid: it carries no ticks and does not indicate the origin or scale.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/scene/Scene.html#pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene.save_html\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene.save_html\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">save_html</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">path</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd></dd>", "a[href=\"#the-duty\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">The duty<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#the-duty\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">TurbineDuty.from_states</span></code> takes a medium, a mass flow, the inlet total state,\nthe outlet pressure and the shaft speed. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">TurbineDuty.from_stations</span></code> takes\nthe same from two network stations. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">fluid</span></code> is a CoolProp name, a\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">thermo.Fluid</span></code>, or any <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">thermo.EquationOfState</span></code>.</p><p>The duty reports the isentropic head <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">isentropic_head</span></code>, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pressure_ratio</span></code>, the\nspouting velocity <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">c0</span> <span class=\"pre\">=</span> <span class=\"pre\">sqrt(2*\u0394h_s)</span></code>, the inlet and isentropic-outlet flows\nand densities, the specific speed <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Ns</span></code>, and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">blade_jet_ratio(D)</span></code> and\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">specific_diameter(D)</span></code> for a candidate diameter.</p>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 600, interactive: false,
                onShow(instance) {MathJax.typesetPromise([instance.popper]).then(() => {});},
            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
